IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`
IMPORT `ssc7-12ze`

-- Tests for Part 12ZE (ss 171ZZ16-171ZZ24).  Every expected value is written beside its assertion from the
-- text of the Act (src:4130-4251), before the run, and is never copied from the code's output.
-- ss 171ZZ17-171ZZ24 tests are derived from the 12ZD tests by work/tr_ze.py with the numbers of the 12ZE text
-- (12 weeks, 68 weeks) put in by hand; ss 171ZZ16 tests below are hand-written.
-- Figures that regulations or other Acts supply (the lower earnings limit, the prescribed rate and number of
-- weeks, the day s 63(3) WRA 2012 comes fully into force) are ARBITRARY TEST INPUTS here, not law.
-- Calendar facts used: 1 January 2026 is a Thursday, so 3 January 2026 is a Saturday, 4 January a Sunday and
-- 15 March 2026 a Sunday.

§ `Tests for Part 12ZE`

§§ `Fixtures`

`s 171ZZ16 test person` MEANS Person WITH
    `date of birth` IS Date 1 1 1990
    `sex` IS Man
    `marital status` IS `married`
    `date of attaining pensionable age` IS Date 1 1 2057

GIVEN began IS A DATE
      ended IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN Employment
`s 171ZZ16 test employment` MEANS Employment WITH
    `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ16 test person`
    `the kind of employer` IS `a company or other body corporate`
    `the employment began on` IS began
    `the employment ended on` IS ended
    `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE
    `held in an office` IS FALSE
    `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE

GIVEN careStart IS A DATE
      kind IS A BOOLEAN
      lastDay IS A DATE
      relationship IS A BOOLEAN
      weeks IS A NUMBER
      entitledToBe IS A BOOLEAN
      earnings IS A NUMBER
      regs3 IS A BOOLEAN
      atBeginning IS A BOOLEAN
      continuous IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case`
`s 171ZZ16 test case` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(2) the person's case` WITH
    `the employment` IS `s 171ZZ16 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING
    `the child's date of birth` IS Date 1 1 2026
    `the day the neonatal care started` IS careStart
    `the care is of a prescribed medical or palliative kind` IS kind
    `the last day of uninterrupted care` IS lastDay
    `the person satisfies the prescribed conditions as to a parental or other personal relationship with the child` IS relationship
    `weeks of continuous employment ending with the relevant week` IS weeks
    `at the end of the relevant week the person was entitled to be in that employment` IS entitledToBe
    `normal weekly earnings in pounds for the 8 weeks ending with the relevant week` IS earnings
    `regulations prescribe the condition in subsection (3)` IS regs3
    `at the beginning of the week or period the person is in the employment` IS atBeginning
    `that employment has been continuous from the end of the relevant week` IS continuous

-- Child born Thursday 1 Jan 2026; care starts Monday 5 Jan 2026 and lasts without interruption to 12 Jan 2026 (7 days after
-- the 5th); prescribed kind; relationship met; 52 weeks; entitled to be in the employment; earnings 150 against the test limit 100;
-- no regulations under subsection (3).
`s 171ZZ16 test base` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test no relationship` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) FALSE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test care not prescribed kind` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test care started on day 29` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 30 1 2026) TRUE (Date 6 2 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test care started on day 28` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 29 1 2026) TRUE (Date 5 2 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test care lasted 6 days` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 11 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test 25 weeks` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 25 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test 26 weeks` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 26 TRUE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test not entitled to be in the employment` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 FALSE 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test earnings 99.99` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 99.99 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test earnings 100` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 100 FALSE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test regs3 and satisfied` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 TRUE TRUE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test regs3 not in employment at start` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 TRUE FALSE TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test regs3 not continuous` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- No regulations under (3), so the (3) facts are irrelevant even if false.
`s 171ZZ16 test no regs3 and (3) facts false` MEANS `s 171ZZ16 test case` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE (Date 12 1 2026) TRUE 52 TRUE 150 FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- An arbitrary test lower earnings limit of 100 pounds a week, and arbitrary days for s 63(3) WRA 2012.
`s 171ZZ16 test LEL` MEANS 100
`s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` MEANS Date 1 1 2020
`s 171ZZ16 test WRA day future` MEANS Date 1 1 2030

§§ `s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) seven days`

-- Care starts Mon 5 Jan 2026; the seven days begin the day after (6 Jan) and so end 12 Jan.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) the care has continued without interruption for at least seven days` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 11 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) the care has continued without interruption for at least seven days` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 12 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(a)(ii) the care has continued without interruption for at least seven days` (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 13 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ16(4) neonatal care`

-- Child born 1 Jan 2026: the 28 days begin 2 Jan and end 29 Jan; care that starts on 29 Jan starts before the end, 30 Jan does not.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` TRUE (Date 29 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` TRUE (Date 30 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not of a prescribed medical or palliative kind
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(4) the care is neonatal care` FALSE (Date 5 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZZ16(2)(b) to (d), one paragraph at a time`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` 25 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(b) the person has been in employment for at least 26 weeks` 26 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(c) the person was entitled to be in that employment` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 99.99 100 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 100 100 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2)(d) the normal weekly earnings are not less than the lower earnings limit` 100.01 100 EQUALS TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ16(3) a prescribed condition`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(3) any condition prescribed under this subsection is satisfied` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) omitted`

-- care that "starts before the day": the day before is before, the day itself is not
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(7) paragraph (c) of subsection (2) is omitted` (Date 2 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week`

`s 171ZZ16 test no entitlement` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS FALSE
`s 171ZZ16 test SMP` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS TRUE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS FALSE
`s 171ZZ16 test SPP birth` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS TRUE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS FALSE
`s 171ZZ16 test SPP adoption` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS TRUE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS FALSE
`s 171ZZ16 test SAP` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS TRUE
`s 171ZZ16 test SMP and SAP` MEANS `s 171ZZ16(6) the person's entitlements in respect of the child` WITH `entitled to statutory maternity pay under section 164` IS TRUE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA (birth)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory paternity pay under section 171ZB (adoption)` IS FALSE, `entitled to statutory adoption pay under section 171ZL` IS TRUE
-- The expected week of confinement is Sunday 15 - Saturday 21 March 2026.  The 14th week before it begins 14 weeks (98 days) earlier,
-- Sunday 8 Dec 2025, so the week immediately preceding that one is Sunday 30 Nov - Saturday 6 Dec 2025.
`s 171ZZ16 test expected week` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 15 3 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 3 2026
`s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 7 6 2025
`s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 8 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 14 6 2025
`s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` MEANS Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 15 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 21 6 2025

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SMP` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 30 11 2025, `the last day` IS Date 6 12 2025)
-- (b), (c), (d): the same week as the relevant week of s 171ZA(2), s 171ZB(2), s 171ZL(2) in that case
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SPP birth` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 7 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SPP adoption` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 8 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 14 6 2025)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SAP` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 15 6 2025, `the last day` IS Date 21 6 2025)
-- (e) any other case: the week immediately before the one in which the care starts.  Care starts Mon 5 Jan 2026; its week is Sun 4 - Sat 10 Jan; the one before is Sun 28 Dec 2025 - Sat 3 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test no entitlement` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 28 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2026)
-- care starting on a Sunday (4 Jan 2026): its week is Sun 4 - Sat 10 Jan, so again 28 Dec - 3 Jan; on Saturday 3 Jan: week 28 Dec - 3 Jan, so 21 - 27 Dec
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test no entitlement` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 28 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 3 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test no entitlement` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 3 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 21 12 2025, `the last day` IS Date 27 12 2025)
-- two of the entitlements (a) to (d): the text does not say which governs
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SMP and SAP` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- regulations prescribe another period for the week
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(6) the relevant week` `s 171ZZ16 test SMP` `s 171ZZ16 test expected week` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZA` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZB` `s 171ZZ16 test week from 171ZL` (Date 5 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ16(1) and (2), the whole entitlement`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test base` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(2) the conditions are satisfied` `s 171ZZ16 test base` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` EQUALS TRUE
-- (a)(i) fails alone
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test no relationship` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4) fails alone: not a prescribed kind of care; care starting on day 29
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test care not prescribed kind` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test care started on day 29` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test care started on day 28` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(ii) fails alone: care lasted only 6 days after the start
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test care lasted 6 days` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b): 25 weeks fails, 26 suffices
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test 25 weeks` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test 26 weeks` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c): not entitled to be in the employment; omitted if the care started before the WRA day
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test not entitled to be in the employment` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test not entitled to be in the employment` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day future` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d): 99.99 fails, 100 suffices
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test earnings 99.99` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test earnings 100` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3): a condition prescribed under subsection (3), met and unmet
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test regs3 and satisfied` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test regs3 not in employment at start` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test regs3 not continuous` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test no regs3 and (3) facts false` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- regulations under s 171ZZ17(4) modify or disapply a condition: the text alone cannot answer
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ16(1) the person is entitled to statutory neonatal care pay` `s 171ZZ16 test base` `s 171ZZ16 test LEL` `s 171ZZ16 test WRA day past` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ17 notice`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no notice: "only if the person gives notice", whatever s 171ZZ16(1) says
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` NOTHING FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice given but s 171ZZ16(1) not covered / no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(1) the person is entitled to payments for the weeks` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) writing is required only if the payer asks
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ17(3) the notice satisfies the requirement as to writing` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 171ZZ18 liability`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ18(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory neonatal care pay` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not an employer in the s 171ZZ16(2)(b), (e) sense: s 171ZZ18(3) lets regulations make the Commissioners liable, so not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ18(1) the person is liable to make payments of statutory neonatal care pay` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the duty as a regulative rule: the liable person pays 100 and the duty is FULFILLED (no time limit in the text)
#TRACE `s 171ZZ18(1) the duty to make the payments` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 171ZZ18 the person liable to make the payments` DOES `s 171ZZ18 makes a payment of statutory neonatal care pay` 100 AT 1

§§ `s 171ZZ19 rate and period of pay`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(1) the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay in pounds` (JUST 100) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(1) the weekly rate of statutory neonatal care pay in pounds` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): rate 100; 2 weeks of a prescribed 2 within the qualifying period
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 2 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST 100
-- more weeks than the prescribed number: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 3 2 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- weeks not within the qualifying period: outside the grant
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(2) the pay payable for the weeks chosen in pounds` 100 2 2 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3) "not less than 12"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 11 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 12 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(3) the prescribed number of weeks is allowed` 13 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (5) "at least 68 weeks beginning with the date of the child's birth": 68 weeks is 476 days; 1 Jan 2026 + 475 days is 21 Apr 2027
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 21 4 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 20 4 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not beginning with the date of the birth
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(5) the qualifying period is allowed` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 2 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 31 12 2027) (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (6), (7)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(6) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(7) the person is liable to pay for the statutory pay week whether or not the contract existed before` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (8)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(8) the pay is payable for the statutory pay week` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (10) one seventh of the weekly rate
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(10) the daily rate in pounds` 70 EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(10) the daily rate in pounds` 7 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(10) the daily rate in pounds` 0 EQUALS 0
-- (11) a week is any period of seven days, both ends counted
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 6 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 8 1 2026) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 8 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the period is a statutory pay week` (Period WITH `the first day` IS Date 1 1 2026, `the last day` IS Date 7 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ19(11) the week convention` EQUALS `any period of 7 days`

§§ `s 171ZZ20 contracting out`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(1) the agreement is void to that extent` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(1) the agreement is void to that extent` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(1) the agreement is void to that extent` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(1) the agreement is void to that extent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ20(2) the agreement authorising deductions is not void by virtue of subsection (1)(a)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 171ZZ21 contractual remuneration`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(1) the entitlement affects the person's right to contractual remuneration` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(a) liability 300 less remuneration paid 100 leaves 200; paid 300 or more leaves nothing
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay that remains` 300 100 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay that remains` 300 300 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay that remains` 300 400 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(a) the liability to pay statutory neonatal care pay that remains` 300 0 EQUALS 300
-- (2)(b) the same the other way round
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 200 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ21(2)(b) the liability to pay contractual remuneration that remains` 500 600 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 171ZZ22 Crown employment`

-- the same answer whoever the employer is
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `a company or other body corporate` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `an individual` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `a government department, public authority or other body of persons` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ22 the provisions of this Part apply to the person` `the Crown` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ23 special classes`

#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) needs both "prescribed employment" and continental shelf operations
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ23(1) regulations may modify this Part in its application to the person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 171ZZ24 supplementary`

-- (1) "employer": liable under s 6, or would be but for 6(1)(b) or the employee's being under 16
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- would be liable but for age, but s 173(a) says the employee is not under 16: no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- would be liable but for age, and s 173(a) does not answer: not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- none of the limbs: "means a person who ..." says no
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the person is the employer of the employee` FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1) "modifications includes additions, omissions and amendments"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ24(1) an addition` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ24(1) an omission` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ24(1) an amendment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the change is a modification` `s 171ZZ24(1) another kind of change` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1) "prescribed means prescribed by regulations"
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the matter is prescribed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(1) the matter is prescribed` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2) "employee": in Great Britain, under a contract of service or in an office, with earnings
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZZ16 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` (`s 171ZZ16 test employment` (Date 1 1 2025) NOTHING) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ16 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE, `held in an office` IS TRUE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ16 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS FALSE, `held in an office` IS FALSE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(2) the person is an employee` (Employment WITH `the employee` IS `s 171ZZ16 test person`, `the kind of employer` IS `the Crown`, `the employment began on` IS Date 1 1 2025, `the employment ended on` IS NOTHING, `held under a contract of service` IS TRUE, `held in an office` IS FALSE, `carried on in Great Britain` IS FALSE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5) week: Sunday-start unless regulations prescribe otherwise.  Wed 7 Jan 2026's week begins Sunday 4 Jan 2026.
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(5) the week convention` EQUALS `a period of 7 days beginning with Sunday or another prescribed period`
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 4 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 4 1 2026)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 3 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 12 2025)
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(5) the first day of the week containing the day` (Date 7 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) average weekly earnings: 800 over 8 weeks is 100; a prescribed other calculation, or no weeks, is not covered
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 FALSE EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 8 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 171ZZ24(6) the person's normal weekly earnings in pounds` 800 0 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

